      "attack_scenario": "1) A Tokenomics instance (or proxy pointing to it) is deployed but not yet initialized.\n2) Attacker monitors mempool for deployment / proxy creation.\n3) Before the legitimate initializer transaction, attacker calls `initializeTokenomics(...)` with valid non-zero addresses (they can set `_treasury`, `_depository`, `_dispenser`, `_ve`, and registries to attacker-controlled contracts).\n4) `owner` is set to the attacker.\n5) Attacker can now: (a) call `changeManagers()` to point `treasury/depository/dispenser` to malicious contracts, (b) call `changeTokenomicsImplementation()` to set an arbitrary implementation slot used by `checkpoint()` checks, and (c) generally control protocol incentive accounting and any downstream fund flows performed by the managers (treasury/dispenser/depository).",
      "suggested_fix": "Restrict initialization to a trusted deployer/proxy mechanism:\n- If used behind a proxy, add an `onlyProxy` / `onlyDelegateCall` style modifier for `initializeTokenomics()` (e.g., OpenZeppelin `initializer` + `onlyInitializing` pattern or a custom check that `address(this)` is the proxy and/or an immutable implementation address).\n- Alternatively, require an explicit `owner` parameter and set `owner = _owner` with `require(msg.sender == deployer)`.\n- Best practice: initialize atomically during proxy deployment (constructor of proxy or factory) so no external party can front-run."
